      "problem": "Solve for $x$ where $2x - y = 5y - z.$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $x,$ so we will treat the other variables $y$ and $z$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $x.$\n\nFirst, we add $y$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x - y &= 5y - z \\[5pt]\n\t\t2x - y + y &= 5y - z + y \\[5pt]\n\t\t2x &= 6y - z\n\t}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we divide both sides by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x &= 6y - z \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2x} 2 &= \\dfrac{6y - z} {2} \\[5pt]\n\t\tx &= \\dfrac{6y - z} {2}\n\t}\n$$",
